url: "https://github.com/xavierbasilbritto-hub/pLIN-plasmid-classification"
abstract: >-
  pLIN (plasmid Lineage Identification Number) is a hierarchical,
  permanent, reference-free classification system for bacterial
  plasmid genomes integrated with antimicrobial resistance gene
  surveillance. It assigns each plasmid a six-position code
  (A.B.C.D.E.F) based on tetranucleotide composition distances
  and hierarchical clustering. Features include automatic Inc
  group detection (91.1% accuracy, 28 Inc/Rep groups), plasmid mobility
  prediction, outbreak detection with clinical risk stratification,
  CRISPR spacer-based host inference, and an interactive Streamlit
  web GUI with AMRFinderPlus integration. Reference database of
  78,902 plasmids with 33,143 unique pLIN codes.
keywords:
